        "source": "def summarize_values(values):\n    n = len(values)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    contrib = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        x = values[i]\n        p = 2*x + 1*x*x + 1*x*x*x\n        g = 1\n        if i == 0:\n            extra = 0\n        else:\n            extra = g * x * values[i-1]\n        contrib.append(p + extra)\n    for _ in range(3):\n        for i in range(1, n):\n            contrib[i] = contrib[i] + contrib[i-1]\n    return contrib[-1]\n\ndef readout(summary):\n    return summary\n\ndef investigate(context, acquire):\n    return readout(summarize_values(context[\"values\"]))\n",
        "scope": "Replaced the identity readout with a fixed polynomial-plus-lag contribution and three cumulative-sum passes, matching the synthetic integer sequence family.",
        "change": "summarize_values now computes p(x)=2x+x^2+x^3 plus g*x*previous with g=1, then applies three cumulative sums and returns the last entry; readout and investigate remain pass-through.",
